  "title": "How to Buy a Business with $0 Down (No, Really)",
  "date": "2025-04-04T14:31:28.757Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n How to Buy a Business with $0 Down (No, Really)\nHi Sara,\nWant to buy a business without spending a dime of your own money? It sounds like a scam, right? Like some late-night infomercial: \u201cThis one weird trick will make you a millionaire!\u201d\nI promise you\u2014it\u2019s not.\u00a0\nBut before we get ahead of ourselves, let\u2019s start with what doesn\u2019t work:\n\u274c Convincing a seller to finance 100% of the deal (good luck with that).\n\u274c Finding a \u201cfree\u201d business (if you\u2019ve found one, it\u2019s probably a terrible deal).\n\u274c Manifesting a business into existence (if only it were that easy).\nWhat does work is using an SBA 7(a) loan strategically.\u00a0\nThis program is already a game-changer in business acquisitions, offering financing up to 90%.\u00a0\nBut what if I told you that, in some cases, you can finance 100% of a deal\u2014without putting in a single dollar of your own cash?\nHere\u2019s the play:\n\u279d The SBA requires buyers to put down 10%, right? Well, some lenders will accept a seller note\u2014a loan from the seller themselves\u2014as that 10%.\n\u279d If structured correctly (meaning the note follows SBA rules, like a 24-month standby period), the bank treats it like a cash down payment.\n\u279d Result? You just bought a business with no money out of pocket.\nBut Here\u2019s the Catch...\n\u279d Not all banks do this. You need a preferred SBA lender who actually understands these deals.\n\n \u279d Your Letter of Intent (LOI) matters. If you try to sneak this in last minute, the seller will be less than thrilled. Transparency is key.\n\n \u279d \u201c$0 down\u201d doesn\u2019t mean \u201cfree.\u201d You still need funds for closing costs, loan origination fees, legal fees, and diligence expenses.\nThe Takeaway?\nThere\u2019s an absolute wave of business owners looking to retire\u2014millions of them, in fact. The opportunity is massive. But the people who win? They\u2019re the ones who get creative with financing, work with the right banks, and structure deals that actually close.\nIf this kind of deal-making excites you, check out our courses at Deal Academy for expert guidance on running a successful acquisition process.\nTo buying businesses the smart way,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant & Founder of Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers podcast episodes by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
